    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present Genista Cottage, a truly enchanting two-bedroom thatched cottage occupying a wonderfully private setting amid generous, beautifully landscaped gardens of c.069acre. Ideally positioned between the picturesque villages of Ballyboughal and Oldtown, this exceptional home offers all the tranquillity and charm of country living while remaining within easy reach of Dublin Airport, Swords and the wider Dublin area.\n\nLovingly maintained by its current owners, Genista Cottage is presented in walk-in condition and combines the warmth and character of a traditional Irish cottage with the comfort required for modern living. Its distinctive thatched roof, inviting interiors and remarkable gardens create a home of rare appeal—one that feels immediately welcoming from the moment you arrive.\n\nThe accommodation is arranged over two levels and begins with an entrance hall leading to a charming living room, an inviting space at the heart of the cottage. A separate kitchen provides a practical and well-appointed setting for everyday living, while an adjoining utility room offers valuable additional storage and functionality. Upstairs, two comfortable bedrooms are positioned off the landing together with a shower room.\n\nOutside, the gardens are an outstanding feature of the property. Generous in scale and thoughtfully landscaped, they have been designed to capture the romance and informality of a traditional country cottage garden. Colourful planting, established flowers and secluded “secret garden” areas combine to create a series of beautiful outdoor spaces, each with its own atmosphere and charm.\n\nBeyond the more intimate planted gardens are extensive lawned areas offering wonderful space for recreation, gardening and outdoor entertaining. These grounds may also offer scope for further development, subject to the necessary planning permission. A secondary access to the gardens is available adding further versatility to the overall site.\n\nTwo garden rooms are discreetly positioned within the grounds and offer excellent flexibility for use as home offices, creative studios, hobby rooms or peaceful retreats. An active greenhouse will particularly appeal to gardening enthusiasts and complements the productive and carefully nurtured nature of the gardens.\n\nGenista Cottage presents a rare opportunity to acquire an exceptionally charming country home in a convenient North County Dublin location. Equally suited to those seeking a peaceful permanent residence, an idyllic retreat or a distinctive home with space to work and create, this is a property that must be experienced to be fully appreciated.\n\nLocation\n\nGenista Cottage enjoys an attractive rural position between the welcoming villages of Ballyboughal and Oldtown, two established communities surrounded by the rich countryside of North County Dublin.\n\nBallyboughal offers a strong sense of village life, with local shops and services, a pharmacy, national school, church and community facilities. The village is also home to Ballyboughal GFC, a pitch and putt club, boxing and a variety of active community organisations. Oldtown provides further everyday amenities, including a national school and local sporting and community facilities.\n\nA wider selection of shops, restaurants, schools and recreational amenities can be found in nearby Swords and Ashbourne. The surrounding area offers an excellent choice of sporting pursuits, with local GAA clubs, golf courses, equestrian facilities, athletics and countryside walking all readily accessible.\n\nDespite its peaceful rural setting, the property is conveniently positioned for access to the M1 and M50 motorway networks, providing connections to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport and the greater Dublin region. Swords, Ashbourne, Balbriggan and the coastal villages of North County Dublin are also within comfortable driving distance.\n\nGenista Cottage offers the best of both worlds: an idyllic country setting with space, privacy and natural beauty, together with excellent accessibility to village amenities and major transport routes."
      },
